Thinking in components meant I had to plan the props before writing any markup, instead of writing HTML first and bolting on JS behavior after like I did in earlier tasks. The Modal was the clearest example — three completely different dialogs (welcome, delete-confirm, info) all come from one function, just called with different title/message/confirmText each time, so I never copy-pasted modal markup anywhere. Reusing createButton() inside createModal() itself also showed me real composition — a component built from another component, not just from raw HTML. Chhoti si cheez jo maine seekhi: bugs get way easier to isolate this way too, because if the Danger button looked wrong, I only had to check .btn-danger, not scroll through one giant page of markup.
